A single loop iteration can call several functions:

def enter_room(n):
    print("You enter room", n)

def check_for_enemy():
    print("No enemies here.")

for i in range(1, 4):
    enter_room(i)
    check_for_enemy()

This builds a three-room walk-through with almost no repetition in the calling code.

